IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fhog-grant`
IMPORT `fhog-cases-grant`
IMPORT `fhog-qa`

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (fhog-qa.l4): every exported question, for its one
-- role and every situation.
--
-- The layer has one role, so there is no other role to ask a question for. Each question that takes a situation input
-- is asked with FALSE (the situation does not hold) and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise
-- for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it is an assumed term"). Where
-- the situation holds, each question is asked on the baseline's facts, with the answer worked by hand and also asserted
-- equal to the baseline export's own answer.
--
-- The facts reuse the baseline's fixtures (fhog-cases-grant.l4, imported for its definitions only: an imported
-- module's assertions are not run): Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract (c051) and Jake's apartment off the plan
-- (k074), with the baseline's labelled assumptions. Expected values are written by hand from the deposited text, never
-- copied from the output.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

`as the buyer` MEANS `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia`

§§ `The situation holds: the answer is the baseline's`

-- ss 3, 7: a de facto partner of 3 years counts; of 1 year does not; a husband separated for good does not.
#ASSERT `Does this person count as my spouse or de facto partner` `as the buyer` TRUE `a de facto partner of 3 years who owned a home` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does this person count as my spouse or de facto partner` `as the buyer` TRUE `a de facto partner of 1 year who owned a home` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this person count as my spouse or de facto partner` `as the buyer` TRUE `a separated husband who owned a home` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does this person count as my spouse or de facto partner` `as the buyer` TRUE `Liam, as Chloe's partner` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this person my spouse or de facto partner` `Liam, as Chloe's partner`)

-- s 9A.
#ASSERT `Am I old enough for the grant` `as the buyer` `a 17-year-old` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I old enough for the grant` `as the buyer` `a 17-year-old the Commissioner has exempted` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I old enough for the grant` `as the buyer` `Chloe at 24` EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I old enough` `Chloe at 24`)
-- ss 7B, 10: one citizen is enough for a couple.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion` `as the buyer` `a temporary visa holder` `a temporary visa holder buying alone` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion` `as the buyer` `a temporary visa holder` `a temporary visa holder buying with Jake` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion` `as the buyer` `a permanent visa holder who has not shown an intention to stay` `a temporary visa holder buying alone` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `a permanent visa holder who has not shown an intention to stay` `a temporary visa holder buying alone`)
-- s 11.
#ASSERT `Am I free of the bar on a second grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who has received a grant before` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I free of the bar on a second grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who received a grant and paid it back under its conditions` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I free of the bar on a second grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer whose wife received a grant` EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I free of the second grant bar` `a buyer whose wife received a grant`)
-- s 12.
#ASSERT `Am I a first home owner for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who lived in a home of their own for 2 years` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I a first home owner for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who owned an investment flat but never lived in it` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I a first home owner for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer whose de facto partner of 3 years owned a home` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I a first home owner for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer separated for good from a husband who owned a home` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I a first home owner for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who lived in their own home for 5 months` EQUALS `yes if` (`Have I never owned a home that counts` `a buyer who lived in their own home for 5 months`)
-- s 13.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who moves in 13 months after completion` `a 2027 buyer over the cap` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements for the grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer who moves in 13 months after completion with 18 months approved` `a 2027 buyer over the cap` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements for the grant` `as the buyer` `a co-buyer who never lives there, exempted` `a lone co-buyer who never lives there, exempted` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I meet the residence requirements for the grant` `as the buyer` `a co-buyer who never lives there, exempted` `Jake with a co-buyer who never lives there, exempted` EQUALS `yes if` (`Do I meet the residence requirements` `a co-buyer who never lives there, exempted` `Jake with a co-buyer who never lives there, exempted`)
#ASSERT `How many months must I live in my first home` `as the buyer` `Jake at 35` EQUALS `months` 6
#ASSERT `How many months must I live in my first home` `as the buyer` `a buyer who lives there 4 months with 4 months approved` EQUALS `months` 4
#ASSERT `How many months must I live in my first home` `as the buyer` `Jake at 35` EQUALS `months` (`my required residence months` `Jake at 35`)
#ASSERT `Within how many months after completion must I move into my first home` `as the buyer` `Jake at 35` EQUALS `months` 12
#ASSERT `Within how many months after completion must I move into my first home` `as the buyer` `a buyer who moves in 13 months after completion with 18 months approved` EQUALS `months` 18
#ASSERT `Within how many months after completion must I move into my first home` `as the buyer` `Chloe at 24` EQUALS `months` (`my takeup months` `Chloe at 24`)
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer convicted under the Act` `a 2027 buyer over the cap` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer holding as trustee` `a 2027 buyer over the cap` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` `as the buyer` `a buyer holding part as trustee under Help to Buy` `a 2027 buyer over the cap` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` `as the buyer` `Jake at 35` `k074: Jake's application after settlement` EQUALS `yes if` (`Am I eligible` `Jake at 35` `k074: Jake's application after settlement`)

